  "body": "When running a WPT[1] which has a `javascript: URL` in HREF of an a element. Suppose `JS URL` should get later, but I got a different result:\r\n\r\n**Gecko**\r\n[inline script 1, end script 1, inline script 2, **JS URL**]\r\n\r\n**Blink, Safari and Edge**\r\n[inline script 1, **JS URL**, end script 1, inline script 2]\r\n\r\nThe spec[2] says\r\n```\r\nIf resource is a request whose url's scheme is \"javascript\"\r\n    Queue a task, on the DOM manipulation task source and associated with the active document of browsingContext.\r\n```\r\n\r\n[1] http://w3c-test.org/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/execution-timing/029.html\r\n[2] Step 13 https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#navigating-across-documents \r\n",
